# MAGIC
# MAGIC **How it works:**
# MAGIC 1. Define a scorer function with `@scorer`
# MAGIC 2. Call `.register(name=...)` to make it available by name
# MAGIC 3. Add the scorer name to `eval/gates.yml` under the appropriate tier
# MAGIC
# MAGIC **Available parameters** (all keyword-only, all optional):
# MAGIC - `inputs` — the raw request dict sent to the agent
# MAGIC - `outputs` — the raw response from the agent
# MAGIC - `expectations` — ground truth / labels from the eval dataset
# MAGIC - `trace` — the full MLflow trace with all spans
# MAGIC
# MAGIC **Return types:**
# MAGIC - `bool`, `int`, `float`, `str` ("yes"/"no") — simple scores
# MAGIC - `Feedback(value=..., rationale=...)` — score with explanation
# MAGIC - `list[Feedback]` — multiple metrics from one scorer

